# Taster of Wares: "you may cast it for as long as you control this creature" (CR 611.2a, 611.2b, 113.8). With the Taster's
# enters trigger on the stack Bot1 shrinks it with Ray of Enfeeblement (power 3 - 4 is no more than Old Man of the Sea's 2) and
# takes it with Old Man. The trigger still resolves under Bot2, who controls one Goblin (the Chomping Changeling) so X is 1, and
# Bot1's Lightning Bolt is exiled - but Bot2 no longer controls the Taster, so "for as long as you control this creature" has
# ended before it began, and Bot1, who never was "you", may not cast the Bolt either, though a Mox Ruby's mana is open.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Old Man of the Sea
Ray of Enfeeblement
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x30

[Bot2 Deck]
